Workers within your supply chain",No,,Yes,"Using anonymous whistleblowing services, such as a helpline or mobile phone app",No,"We monitor via supplier onboarding MS questionnaires, supplier quality audits, modern slavery training, payroll checks for duplicate bank accounts, and review of working condition cases.",No,"Use of third‑party labour providers in higher‑risk countries, including risk of wage withholding or poor working conditions for contract labour.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,Other vulnerable groups,Daily workers reliant on a third‑party labour provider for employment,India,"We investigated an allegation that a labour provider may have withheld worker pay. We reviewed contracts, payroll arrangements and local controls and did not substantiate wage withholding. Control gaps were identified. The labour provider was off‑boarded and replaced following due diligence on a new provider, with ongoing monitoring in place.",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Yes,,,"Our statement shows progress through expanded use of KPIs, including training completion, supplier onboarding and questionnaire coverage, and payroll red flag checks. We strengthened supplier due diligence, enhanced monitoring, and used assurance reviews to drive improvements and inform priorities for future statements.",2026-04-20T09:28:22,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/EcdGzCQG/2026/Slavery and Human Trafficking Statement 2025.pdf
