Tier 3 suppliers and below",Migrants,,United Kingdom,"We are a member of the Seasonal Workers Scheme Taskforce, which works to safeguard the rights of seasonal workers in UK horticulture. In 2025, the Taskforce focused on three priority areas: worker education and grievance mechanisms; responsible recruitment and on-farm practices; and the feasibility of implementing the Employer Pays Principle, which aims to eliminate worker-paid recruitment fees.",National store maintenance suppliers in the UK,Within your own operations,,"Migrants
Other vulnerable groups",Low-paid and low-skilled workers,United Kingdom,"Recognising construction as a key risk area, we assessed three major maintenance suppliers with the Slave-free Alliance, covering both skilled and lower-skilled roles. Reviews of policies, systems and practices identified common gaps, including limited whistleblowing access, lack of worker-facing modern slavery policies, and low awareness. We then worked with suppliers to deliver targeted improvements, including tailored training, better policy access, and clearer reporting channels.",,Yes,,,"We use set KPI's to measure our performance.  We also report on our progress in meeting goals set out in the ""Looking Forward"" section of our previous years statement.",2026-06-29T10:13:19,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/u4EF8k4H/2026/Aldi UK and Ireland Modern Slavery Statement 2025.pdf
