Refugees",,United Kingdom,"Amey continues to use its web-based training accessible to its online employees. For off-line employees we have produced a training and briefing for cascading by supervisors, along with posters and communications materials on what to do, if they have a concern. During 2025, we appointed 5 Anti-Slavery Ambassadors, who act as local champions to embed awareness, promote good practice and support early escalation of concerns.","Supply Chain Risk. In 2025, engagement with supply chain, publishing a new ‘Working with Suppliers’ guide. Business ethics & integrity, human rights & modern slavery formed a key element of the guide.",Within your supply chains,"Tier 1 suppliers
Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below","Migrants
Refugees",,United Kingdom,"During 2025 Amey continued to engage with its supply chain, publishing a new ‘Working with our Suppliers’ guide that aimed to set out the specific commitment Amey makes to its suppliers & the expectation Amey requires from them. Business ethics and integrity, human rights and modern slavery formed a key element of the guide. The guide emphasises that failure to respond to any enquiries from Amey carries consequence for those within the supply chain, ultimately including exclusion as a supplier.","Risk of non-reporting – To reduce the risk of non-reporting or inability to report, Amey has revised its whistleblowing policy and procedure.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,"Migrants
Refugees",,United Kingdom,"To reduce the risk of non-reporting or inability to report, Amey has revised its whistleblowing policy and procedure.",,Yes,,,"The main KPIs in 2025 are:
•Actual incidents raised: nil.
•Potential incidents raised: 2
•Employee training: module updated & rolled out across the business, with monthly tracking of progress
•Screening for duplications in data as a potential indicator
•Percentage of suppliers using Constructionline: 92.
The Working Group established an Action Plan to address ongoing risks across the business & the supply chain.
Amey completed the Government’s Modern Slavery Assessment Tool, with a score of 97%.",2026-04-17T15:52:30,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/jEF0Mxsa/2026/Slavery and Human Trafficking Statement 2025.pdf
