Children",,,"We use geographical and sector risk mapping, contractual safeguards and an Ethical Trading Pledge requiring voluntary employment, safe working conditions and lawful wages. We seek supplier assurances and review compliance statements. We are working towards KPIs and enhanced supply-chain auditing to strengthen monitoring.",Workers producing construction materials for our UK hotel operations may face forced labour or underage labour.,Within your supply chains,Tier 2 suppliers,Children,,,"We use geographical and sector risk mapping, contractual safeguards and an Ethical Trading Pledge requiring voluntary employment, safe working conditions and no forced or underage labour. We seek supplier assurances and review compliance statements. We are working towards KPIs and enhanced supply-chain auditing to strengthen monitoring.",,Yes,,,"Our statement describes progress through refined risk assessments, supply-chain mapping, expanded training and supplier engagement. We monitor supplier compliance through statements and external risk resources. Next steps include KPIs for policy effectiveness, supplier compliance and risk management, enhanced auditing and senior-director oversight. These are planned improvements; no quantified year-on-year results or time-bound targets are reported.",2026-11-02T09:06:58,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/QdEFgv2K/2026/Apex Hospitality Group MS Statement PDF.pdf
