Children",,,"We assess tier‑1 suppliers through 3PRM and strengthen requirements via our Third‑Party Code of Conduct and contract terms. We use audits, corrective action plans and supplier engagement to address findings, and leverage EcoVadis to identify and improve supplier performance. We have launched a human rights risk review to assess mitigations and risk assessments across the lifecycle of a medical device, delivering recommendations in 2026.",Excessive overtime,No,,Yes,"AstraZeneca continues to enhance our policies and governance, including the introduction of a new Global Human Rights Standard, while optimising our third‑party due diligence and monitoring. We are also expanding training and supplier engagement, and progressing targeted initiatives to gain deeper insight into salient human rights risks. Supplier performance improvements are tracked year on year through EcoVadis.",2026-05-05T11:57:41,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/ME4QEkC3/2026/AstraZeneca Modern Slavery Statement 2025.pdf
