Improve understanding and transparency.","Temporary labour supply due to reliance on agency labour, migrant workers within the wider labour market, reduced visibility of worker welfare in agency supply chains & neutral-vendor arrangements.",,,,,,,Procurement and wider supply-chain assurance is an area requiring further development.,,,,,,,,Yes,,,"Our statement demonstrates progress through strengthened governance, formal risk assessments, twice-yearly workforce assurance checks, agency audits and supplier reviews, and targeted training. It also shows continued improvement through actions from the Unseen gap analysis, new performance measures and clear priorities to strengthen procurement, supplier due diligence and wider supply-chain assurance.",2026-10-15T14:03:15,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/VsC3MnK5/2026/Avenues Modern Slavery Statement 25-26.pdf
