Refugees",,United Kingdom,"To mitigate risks associated with product sourcing we develop targeted policies for high risk areas. For example, in 2025, our Construction division developed a solar panel procurement policy to establish permitted purchase rules and reduce supply chain risk.",The risk of the use of low-skilled or migrant labour supplied by subcontractors who are at a higher risk of exploitation.,Within your own operations,,"Migrants
Refugees",,United Kingdom,"Our robust due diligence and risk assessment process includes prequalification criteria, contractual obligations and minimum training standards. We also provide modern slavery training to our suppliers through the Supply Chain Sustainability School (SCSS) and collaborate with industry organisations, peers and platforms to inform best practice.",The risk of ineffective right to work checks.,Within your own operations,,Migrants,,United Kingdom,"Divisions utilise digital technologies to reduce risk, strengthen compliance and safeguard tenants. For example, digital platforms like Chime are used to track operative skills and qualifications prior to site deployment to ensure that only certified professionals are sent to live jobs.",,Yes,,,"We monitor KPIs across training, supplier engagement and whistleblowing reports to identify progress against our efforts to eliminate modern slavery and human trafficking in our business and supply chain.",2026-04-28T11:39:16,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/ENkEMR7y/2026/MS_Modern_Slavery_Statement_2025.pdf
