Through trade unions or other worker representative groups",No,,No,Risks of child labour in India,Within your supply chains,Don't know,Children,,India,"Bayer's Child Care Programme has run for many years in the countries in which we identified the risk of child labour infractions in the seed supply chain - India, Bangladesh and the Philippines and, more recently, Thailand and Indonesia. Via the programme, Bayer raises awareness about this issue among suppliers and clearly communicates its requirements. It involves systematic and repeated inspections of individual seed producers in their fields by local Bayer employees during the growing season.",Risks of child labour in Thailand,Within your supply chains,Don't know,Children,,Thailand,"Bayer's Child Care Programme has run for many years in the countries in which we identified the risk of child labour infractions in the seed supply chain - India, Bangladesh and the Philippines and, more recently, Thailand and Indonesia. Via the programme, Bayer raises awareness about this issue among suppliers and clearly communicates its requirements. It involves systematic and repeated inspections of individual seed producers in their fields by local Bayer employees during the growing season.",Risks of child labour in Indonesia,Within your supply chains,Don't know,Children,,Indonesia,"Bayer's Child Care Programme has run for many years in the countries in which we identified the risk of child labour infractions in the seed supply chain - India, Bangladesh and the Philippines and, more recently, Thailand and Indonesia. Via the programme, Bayer raises awareness about this issue among suppliers and clearly communicates its requirements. It involves systematic and repeated inspections of individual seed producers in their fields by local Bayer employees during the growing season.",,Yes,,,"All reports are investigated. As in previous years, in 2025 there were no confirmed cases of child labour, forced labour, or human trafficking.  1,334 assessments & 100 audits of our suppliers were conducted in 2025 (2024 comparatives are 1,324 and 131.) Bayer is now also utilising an AI web-scraping tool to review suppliers from publicly available information, to analyse their policies and to pick up on externally reported litigation, law enforcement, sanctions and adverse news coverage.",2026-06-10T13:54:15,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/ENsCZbQh/2026/SIGNED MSA FY 2025.pdf
