Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below",Migrants,,,"To assist with sustainability analysis within sectors, regions and companies, we use CONTEXT™, a proprietary model that is accessible to investment teams. We have developed a framework for analysing a company’s human rights due diligence efforts across 5 areas of human rights due diligence. Our engagement strategy aims to identify companies with the most material risks of human rights abuses and work with them to address their approaches to human rights and encourage them to implement the UNGPs.",A risk that our employees could be exploited.,Within your own operations,,Migrants,,,"We manage the risk of modern slavery within our workforce by making sure all new hires possess the legal right to work in their 
respective countries and that their fundamental rights as workers are protected. We conduct pre-employment checks, including right-to-work checks. We require outsourced companies to carry out employment checks and follow the standards set out in our Supplier Code of Conduct. We encourage our suppliers and their subcontractors to provide training 
on worker welfare.","A risk that we could purchase goods and services from companies involved 
in modern slavery.",Within your supply chains,"Tier 1 suppliers
Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below",Migrants,,,"We screen and monitor supplier risk, escalating any issues to relevant subject matter experts for investigation. This screening is carried out before onboarding a new supplier and is subsequently monitored on an ongoing basis. We carried out targeted enhanced due diligence on suppliers assessed as highest risk, based on their total risk scores. 
This included reviewing responses to our business transparency questionnaire and assessing suppliers using a third-party risk 
analytics database.",,Yes,,,"We measure and report on a number of KPIs including: number of instances of modern slavery reported, number of human rights-related engagements across our clients' investment portfolios, completion rate from modern slavery e-learning and number of modern slavery engagements with suppliers.
Over time we will enhance our measurement of assessing the effectiveness of our approach and progress with smarter metrics.",2026-06-30T18:12:52,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/C26VZbuW/2026/Schroders Modern Slavery Statement 2025.pdf
